@startuml
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor User

package "Simple Dashboard" {
  [Overview] as Overview
  [Trades] as TradesUI
  [Weekly Review] as Review
}

package "Spring Boot Trading Core" {
  [Scheduler] as Scheduler
  [Strategy] as Strategy
  [Optional AI Research] as AI
  [Risk Engine] as Risk
  [Execution Engine] as Execution
  [Portfolio State] as Portfolio
}

database "PostgreSQL\nPortfolio + Orders + Trades" as DB
cloud "Market Data" as Market

package "Exchange" {
  interface ExchangePort
  [Paper Exchange] as Paper
  [Kraken] as Kraken
}

User --> Overview
User --> TradesUI
User --> Review
Overview --> Portfolio
TradesUI --> DB
Review --> DB

Scheduler --> Strategy
Market --> Strategy
Market --> Portfolio
Strategy --> AI : optional context
AI --> Risk : trade idea
Strategy --> Risk : trade idea
Portfolio --> Risk : trusted state
Risk --> Execution : approved + sized order
Execution --> ExchangePort
ExchangePort <|.. Paper
ExchangePort <|.. Kraken
Execution --> DB
Portfolio --> DB
Kraken --> Portfolio : balances / orders

note right of Strategy
START SIMPLE
One swing strategy first
BTC / ETH / SOL
AI is optional, not required
end note

note right of Risk
SIMPLE HARD RULES
- no leverage
- fixed risk per trade
- max position size
- daily / weekly loss limit
- max drawdown
- mandatory invalidation / stop
- no new risk when halted
end note

note right of Paper
DEFAULT UNTIL PROVEN
Realistic fees + slippage
Same rules as live mode
end note

note right of Kraken
FIRST LIVE TARGET
Trade-only API key
No withdrawals / transfers
Only allocated capital
end note

note bottom of DB
ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH
Balances, positions, open orders,
fills, P&L and decision history
end note

note bottom of Review
WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW
Did it make money?
Did it beat BTC / ETH hold?
What was max drawdown?
Did any rule break?
Should it keep running?
end note

note bottom
OVERALL PRINCIPLE
Keep it understandable, easy to operate and measurable.
Do not add components, agents or models unless they prove useful.
Market Data -> Strategy -> Risk -> Exchange -> Ledger
end note

@enduml
